# Auto deploy to Git

After finishing a meaningful code/content change for this project (Giara site), **commit and push to `origin/main` without waiting for the user to ask**.

## When to deploy
- UI, copy, branding, config, or feature changes that should live on GitHub
- Do it at the end of the task, once the change works

## When NOT to deploy
- Pure questions / exploration with no file changes
- If the user explicitly says not to push / not to commit
- Do not commit secrets (`.env.local`, credentials, API keys)
- Skip unrelated local experiments unless they are part of the requested work (e.g. leave `test-empresa/`, scratch `scripts/` alone unless asked)

## How
1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` (brief) per normal commit protocol
2. Stage only relevant files
3. Commit with a concise message (HEREDOC)
4. `git push -u origin HEAD` (never force-push)
5. Mention the commit briefly in the reply; no need to ask “¿hago deploy?”
